"""open-progression runtime map-edit data — GENERATED by
re_only/gen_openworld.py. Do not hand-edit; regenerate instead.

Overworld (MAP_00) decompressed AMD grid = 255x255 u16 tile ids, stride 510, in a
heap arena re-decompressed on (some) overworld loads and relocating between boots.
Locate via ANCHOR = vanilla bytes of row 132 x155..174 (never edited/regressed):
grid_base = anchor_addr - ANCHOR_OFF. Tile attr table (512 x u16, movement
semantics, read live per step) located by its vanilla 512-byte prefix.

Two INDEPENDENT toggles select which edits the client applies (ApClient
_openworld_loop): EARLY_GRID_EDITS (early_open_progression) = Cornelia->Duergar foot
pass + Gulg/Crescent<->Ice canoe river; EXTENDED_GRID_EDITS (extended_open_progression)
= Duergar->Western Keep foot trail + Duergar<->Melmond canoe river. CANAL_ATT
(the canal's centre cell, walk+sail) is applied ALWAYS -- the canal is blown
normally; we only make the open canal walkable. Its bridge art is BAKED (see
map_bake), never poked. See memories open-progression-rework, canal-shallows-plan.
"""

ANCHOR_OFF = 132 * 510 + 155 * 2          # 0x1082E
GRID_W, GRID_STRIDE = 255, 510

ANCHOR = bytes.fromhex("440070007100be00bf005400c100a300a400a5006a006b005100e600e700e600f600e70051004700")
ATT_PREFIX = bytes.fromhex("")

